 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling, punctuation and syllables: chi'l on one note, dall' on its own note before al-tro, menuetto, l'alemana (the libretto has l'alemanna), folia in bar 39 (follia in bars 49 and 111; both sung and written in IPA as follia), and vo without its apostrophe in bar 66. In bar 134 the print drops the en of aumentar; the full word is kept. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S24) and the IPA was checked against Castel. Don Giovanni sings the ten lines, then the last two again, the third and fourth, the last two, the fifth to seventh, and a long ending on d'una decina devi aumentar. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
